From: Ben Bangert <100193+bbangert@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PM / devfreq: px30: start with the userspace governor

Nothing changes the DDR rate at boot: the loader's rate stays until a
rate is written to the userspace governor, so a bad switch can be
undone by a power cycle.
---
 drivers/devfreq/Kconfig    | 1 +
 drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/Kconfig b/drivers/devfreq/Kconfig
index fe9ccaa..f3a4aef 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/Kconfig
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@ config ARM_PX30_DMC_DEVFREQ
 		(COMPILE_TEST && HAVE_ARM_SMCCC)
 	select DEVFREQ_EVENT_ROCKCHIP_DFI
 	select DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND
+	select DEVFREQ_GOV_USERSPACE
 	select PM_DEVFREQ_EVENT
 	select PM_OPP
 	help
diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
index e7e258c..3d70d79 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
@@ -430,8 +430,12 @@ static int px30_dmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		.initial_freq	= freq,
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the loader's rate until userspace asks for another one; the
+	 * ondemand tunables are still passed for a later governor switch.
+	 */
 	dmc->devfreq = devm_devfreq_add_device(dev, &dmc->profile,
-					       DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND,
+					       DEVFREQ_GOV_USERSPACE,
 					       &dmc->ondemand);
 	if (IS_ERR(dmc->devfreq))
 		return PTR_ERR(dmc->devfreq);
